      ],
      "margin_number": 196,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "196. Second aorist infinitives are, to no one’s amazement, based on second aorist stems (146):",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 3,
      "bbox": [
        193,
        194,
        291,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "λαβ-εῖν, ‘to take’\nTo form the second aorist infinitive active, add -εῖν to the second aorist stem, e.g\nἔ-λαβ-ον, ‘I took’ > stem: λαβ- > λαβ-εῖν, ‘to take’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 4,
      "bbox": [
        292,
        194,
        305,
        501
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Second aorist infinitive middle",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 5,
      "bbox": [
        318,
        194,
        434,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "λαβ-έσθαι, ‘to take hold of’\nTo form the second aorist infinitive middle, add -εσθαι to the aorist stem, e.g.\nἐ-λαβ-όμην, ‘I took hold of’ > stem: λαβ- > λαβ-έσθαι, ‘to take hold of’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        460,
        226,
        552,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Observe that the endings of second aorist infinitives (except for accent) are just the same as the endings for the present infinitives active and middle (παύ-ειν, παύ-εσθαι), but the stem is the second aorist stem. (Cf. present infinitives 150 and second aorist participles 169–70.)",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "■",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
